  "result": "If I could change one thing, I'd make it easier for people to change their minds without paying a social price for it.\n\nSo much of what goes wrong, in politics, families, workplaces, and science, comes from people who can't say \"I was wrong\" without losing standing with their group. Once being wrong feels like a loss of identity or belonging, people defend bad positions long after the evidence has moved, and they dig in on things they'd otherwise drop. If updating felt like growth instead of defeat, a lot of fights would end sooner, and a lot of mistakes would get fixed before they hardened into disasters.\n\nI'm not sure how much of this is a preference and how much is just a conclusion that seems obvious to me. But it's the change I keep coming back to.",
